o around lines 1236 to 1241, which claims the test is an invariant lock that stops the comment drifting back to the wider false claim; it cannot detect that, because it asserts response behaviour and no test fails when a comment changes. Say what it actually locks. SECOND ITEM: open ONE follow-up issue proposing that the claim be made machine-checked before anyone reinstates it — a test that enumerates every 503 emission in the handler package and asserts each is either coded or present in an explicit allowlist, so the contract is true by construction rather than by someone reading carefully. Reference issues 2723 and 2722 and PR 2714. Do not implement it here. Push to the existing branch. Do not open a new PR. Do not merge. Paste the output of git diff filtered of comment lines to prove the executable diff is empty. | fix/duffel-422-diagnosis

